# i18n foundations (always-on)

Full detail: `docs/i18n.md`.

## UI locale ≠ learning language

- Never use a single unqualified `language` field for both app chrome locale and “what I’m studying.”
- Prefer explicit names in schemas/settings: e.g. `uiLocale`, `learningLanguage`, `contentLocale`.
- Target UI pair when localization ships: `en` + `es-419` (Latin American Spanish). `pt-BR` is a later candidate.

## Code habits (even before an i18n library)

- No user-visible English (or any UI) copy inside `packages/core`.
- API errors: prefer stable **codes**; clients map codes to localized strings.
- Avoid sentence concatenation (`"Hello, " + name`). Use single templates with placeholders when adding messages.
- Persist timestamps in UTC/ISO; format for display with `Intl` and the active UI locale.
- Learning content (decks, cards, mnemonics): plan/include a content language/locale in new models.

## Do not

- Block core feature work on full marketing translations.
- Over-split `es-MX` / `es-AR` before `es-419` exists.
